 122: WHY THE CHECKSTOP AND ME-SET ROWS EXIST.  MSR is 0 on `T step`, `T cont` and `again`; `T me` sets MSR[ME] (0x1000).  On the
 123: first three, arm (c) deleted or inverted falls to the checkstop fallback, which parks identically -- same pc, SRR0 and
 124: next_ic -- and differs only by its text (the `chkstop` rows).  And arm (c) ordered below arm (d), or conditioned on ME clear,
 125: differs only when ME is set (the `T me` session, which drives arm (d)'s tested bit at the -T halt).  Both were added by the
 126: pre-table check, before the test-variant table ran.  Arm (a)'s guard conjoined with an ME-clear test differs only on a
 127: read-ahead with ME set (`T ra me` and the three unaligned `m` sessions), and conjoined with an ME-set test only on one with ME
 128: clear (`T ra`, `T ra odd`, `T ra o2`, `T ra o3`); an arm (c) that sends an ME-set halt to bad: only by its UNIMPLEMENTED text (`T
 129: me unimpl`, and from repair 8 the unimpl rows of the four ME-set read-ahead sessions).  An arm (c) that sends an ME-set halt to the
 130: checkstop fallback differs only by the checkstop line, so `T me` and `T ra me` carry a chkstop row (`T me chkstop`, `T ra me
 131: chkstop`; the shape-grid check before table 3 found that composition, all three cloud seats).
 132: 
 133: CLAUSE (e) -- catches (test-variant table 12, artifacts/qhslowifetch/r7_20261105/table12/SCORES.txt, PRETABLE_12.out written before
 134: it; 88 variants on this 249-row probe: 73 red, every one on this probe; 14 green, the predicted fourteen; V12 NOT PREDICTED): the
 135: removed exit reinstated verbatim (B1); a bare return at the arm head (W2) or on every non-read-ahead fetch (D5); goto bad (W3); an
 136: ISI invented in arm (c) (W4); the arm emptied, or skipped by conditioning the read's failure test on running, so the uninitialised
 137: word decodes (W5, D7); arm (c) inverted or deleted (D1, D2: the chkstop rows of the ME-clear -T sessions -- `T cont`, `T step`,
 138: `again`, `T blr` and the four ME-clear read-ahead sessions -- and, where ME is set and the missing park falls to the machine check,
 139: `T me exc` and the pc and srr0 rows of `T me`, `T ra me` and the three unaligned ME-set read-ahead sessions; `T me chkstop` and the
 140: four ME-set read-ahead chkstop rows stay green under both -- this clause said "D1, D2: the chkstop rows", which
 141: LATE_REPLICATIONS_20261105.md row 13 found too broad); arm (c) without its park (D3); arm (b) inverted (D4: `T cont nonex`, `T ra
 142: nonex`, `T ra me nonex`); arm (c) below arm (d), or conditioned on ME clear or on ME set (D8, D13, D14); the read's failure test
 143: made always true (D15: the noT rows and the read-ahead sessions) or inverted (V7: the same rows plus `T cont unimpl` and the pc,
 144: srr0 and exc rows of `T step`, `T me` and `again` -- this clause said "D15, V7: the noT rows and the read-ahead sessions", which
 145: omitted those, LATE_REPLICATIONS_20261105.md row 12; V7 is build-dependent, so these are its table-8 rows); arm (a)'s guard deleted
 146: (W7), and the slow path skipped during read-ahead (D12), by the read-ahead rows; arm (a)'s guard conjoined with ME clear (V8: the
 147: nonex rows of the four ME-set read-ahead sessions) or with ME set (V9: those of the four ME-clear ones); an ME-set halt sent to
 148: bad: (V10: the unimpl rows of `T me` and the four ME-set read-ahead sessions) or to the checkstop fallback (V11: the chkstop rows
 149: of `T me` and the four ME-set read-ahead sessions); MSR[ME] cleared in arm (c) (B1a: `T me msr` and the msr rows of the four ME-set
 150: read-ahead sessions) or in arm (a) (B1b: those four), or set in arm (c) (B1c: the msr rows of `T cont`, `T step`, `again`, `T blr`
 151: and the four ME-clear read-ahead sessions); the checkstop line printed on an ME-clear read-ahead failure while arm (a) still
 152: returns (B2: the chkstop rows of the four ME-clear read-ahead sessions); arm (b)'s aligned compare reverted to `pc != addr`
 153: (R5_revert: `T blr nonex` and the nonex rows of the six unaligned read-ahead sessions), or its mask narrowed to either low bit
 154: (R5_mask1, R5_mask2: `T blr nonex` and the nonex rows of the four read-ahead sessions whose pc carries the other bit); SRR0 written
 155: in arm (a) (R5_srr0_a: the srr0 rows of all eight read-ahead sessions); the aligned compare's mask widened to bit 2 (R6_mask7: `T
 156: blr nonex`) or to bits 2-3 (R6_mask15: `T blr nonex` and the nonex rows of all eight read-ahead sessions); arm (a)'s guard
 157: conjoined with an alignment test, `cpu->pc == addr` or `!(cpu->pc & 3)` (R6_a_pceq, R6_a_align: the nonex rows of the six unaligned
 158: read-ahead sessions), with a test of pc's bit 1 (R7_a_bit1, codex pass 6's B1: the nonex rows of `T ra o2`, `T ra o2m`, `T ra o3`,
 159: `T ra o3m`) or of bit 0 (R7_a_bit0: those of `T ra odd`, `T ra o1m`, `T ra o3`, `T ra o3m`), with a test refusing an unaligned
 160: read-ahead when ME is set (R7_a_meun, codex's B2, and its De Morgan form R7_x_unme: the nonex rows of `T ra o1m`, `T ra o2m`, `T ra
 161: o3m`) or clear (R7_a_clun and R7_x_uncl: those of `T ra odd`, `T ra o2`, `T ra o3`), or refusing an aligned one when ME is clear
 162: (R7_x_alcl: `T ra nonex`) or set (R7_x_alme: `T ra me nonex`) -- each cell of the grid excluded alone reds exactly its own
 163: sessions; MSR[ME] set or cleared in arm (a) when pc != addr (R7_a_msrset, codex's B3: the msr rows of `T ra odd`, `T ra o2`, `T ra
 164: o3`; R7_a_msrclr: those of `T ra o1m`, `T ra o2m`, `T ra o3m`); SRR0 written, or the checkstop line printed, in arm (a) when pc !=
 165: addr (R7b_a_srr0un, R7b_a_chkun: the six unaligned srr0 or chkstop rows -- each passed all 103 rows before repair 7b), or pc
 166: aligned there (R7b_a_pcalign: their pc rows); the read's failure test disjoined with `cpu->pc != addr` (R7_fail_unal: the pc, nonex
 167: and addr rows of the six unaligned read-ahead sessions, with the chkstop rows of the ME-clear three and the srr0 rows of the ME-set
 168: three -- their first fetch reads successfully at pc != addr, so the block checkstops at the entry pc (ME clear) or takes a machine
 169: check to 0x200 (ME set), with no halt report either way; this clause listed that widening as FILED -- "no row drives" an unaligned
 170: fetch -- until codex pass 6, R3, pointed at `T ra odd`), or conjoined with MSR[ME], with its complement, with
 171: `translation_readahead` or with `cpu->pc != addr` (R7b_f_me, R7b_f_meclr, R7b_f_ra, R7b_f_unal; never built before table 8 --
 172: LATE_REPLICATIONS_20261105.md rows 33 and 41): a failure the conjunct refuses skips the block and decodes the uninitialised ib, so
 173: which rows red is stack-decided, as for W5 and D7, and each reddened only sessions whose failing fetch it refuses, as PRETABLE_8
 174: and PRETABLE_9 predicted; and a halt sent from arm (c) to bad: at pc != addr with ME set (R8_c_meun_bad, codex pass 7's F1: the
 175: unimpl rows of `T ra o1m`, `T ra o2m` and `T ra o3m` -- it passed all 129 rows before repair 8) or with ME clear (R8_c_clun_bad:
 176: those of `T ra odd`, `T ra o2` and `T ra o3`, and `T blr unimpl`, which alone caught it before); and a toggle at the top of the
 177: failed-read block conditioned on pc's low bits -- MSR[ME] at 01, 10, 00 or 11 (R9_tog_me1, codex pass 8's B1, and R9_tog_me2: `T
 178: blr o1 msr`, `T blr o2 msr`; R9_tog_me0: the msr rows of `T cont`, `T step`, `T me` and `again`; R9_tog_me3: `T blr msr`), or SRR0
 179: at 01 (R9_tog_srr0_1: `T blr o1 srr0`) -- which the two-entry read-ahead sessions undo and the one-entry sessions see (R9_tog_me1,
 180: R9_tog_me2 and R9_tog_srr0_1 passed all 137 rows before repair 9); and an SRR0 toggle there gated on MSR[ME] and pc != addr
 181: (R10_tog_srr0_meun, codex pass 9's B1: the srr0 rows of `T blr m1`, `T blr m2` and `T blr m3`; its isolated members
 182: R10_tog_srr0_me1, _me2 and _me3: one each -- all four passed all 153 rows before repair 10) or on low bits 10 alone
 183: (R10_tog_srr0_2: `T blr o2 srr0` and `T blr m2 srr0`); and an SRR0 toggle there gated on the full pc against addr (R11_tog_full,
 184: codex pass 10's B1: the srr0 rows of all eight partners `T rp` .. `T rp o3m`; its members R11_tog_full_<k><c|m>, gated also on low
 185: bits k and ME: each its own cell's partner -- all nine passed all 177 rows before repair 11).  W5, D7, V7 and D12 ride on the
 186: uninitialised or stale instruction word: which rows red is BUILD-DEPENDENT -- D12 reddened a different set in each of tables 2, 3
 187: and 4, with `T ra nonex` in all three (table4/VERDICT.md), table 5 reddened table 4's set plus `T ra srr0`, table 6 moved D12's,
 188: W5's and D7's sets again within the read-ahead rows (r6_20261105/table6/VERDICT.md), table 7 moved them once more -- W5 lost `T ra
 189: me srr0`, D7 gained it, D12 traded `T ra odd pc` for `T ra me pc` and `T ra srr0` (r7_20261105/table7/VERDICT.md) -- and table 8
 190: again on the same 103 rows: W5 regained `T ra me srr0`, and D12 dropped `T ra pc`, `T ra addr`, `T ra srr0`, `T ra o1m pc` and `T
 191: ra o3 pc` and gained `T ra o2m pc` (r7_20261105/table8/VERDICT.md) -- and tables 9 to 12 again (r7_20261105/table9/VERDICT.md ..
 192: table12/VERDICT.md) -- and the claim is that some row reds.  V12 IS NOT PREDICTED: its outcome depends on the uninitialised fetch
 193: buffer ib -- the stale stack word is decoded on the variant's path, and whether a row reds depends on whether that word decodes as
 194: an implemented instruction.  In table 3 it did on the `T ra` leg and a row reddened, while on the `T ra me` leg every row stayed
 195: green -- read as the word decoding to bad:, which returns quietly during read-ahead, an INFERENCE from the all-green leg and not a
 196: measurement (this sentence stated the decode as fact: LATE_REPLICATIONS_20261105.md row 34); table 4, on the same fix, reddened `T
 197: ra me` and left `T ra` green; table 5 reddened both legs; table 6 the `T ra` and `T ra odd` legs; table 7 every read-ahead leg
 198: except `T ra me` and `T ra o3m`; table 8 every one except `T ra` and `T ra o2`; table 9 every one; table 10 every one except `T
 199: ra`, `T ra me` and `T ra o1m`; table 11 every one except `T ra o2`; table 12 every one except `T ra`.  A red that the stack's
 200: contents decide is counted in neither tally.  Zero-initialising ib (filed) would make the variant deterministically green.  Green,
 201: fourteen: arm (d) or the checkstop fallback edited (D6, D9, D10, V4, V5, V6, and R7_G2_d_msr -- the Gemini seat's pass-6 G2, arm
 202: (d)'s test made `if (cpu->cd.ppc.msr)`) -- MEASURED unreached on pmppc (the window sweep below); arm (b) edited (D11, V2, and
 203: R7_G1_b_lt -- the Gemini seat's G1, the aligned compare made `cpu->pc < addr`) -- with the aligned compare arm (b) is taken only
 204: when the translation moved pc to an exception vector, which no measured session produces; arm (c)'s guard forced true (V3), and the
 205: park tested before arm (b) as well (R5_cb) -- equivalent on every reachable entry, since running is 0 at each; arm (a) restoring
 206: running before its return (R5_arun, and R7b_a_runun, the same write gated on pc != addr) -- disclosed below.  The shape-grid check
 207: before table 3 (r3_20261105/GRID_*.md) and the repair-pass-3 findings, each measured before its adjudication (p3_20261105/table_p3,
 208: DHALT_NOTE.md; the ruling p3_20261105/ADJ_MYTHOS.md), placed the msr rows and `T ra chkstop`; the eight-cell table before repair 7
 209: (r7_20261105/B123_NOTE.md) placed `T ra odd msr` and the five sessions `T ra o1m` .. `T ra o3m`; repair 7b's measurement (the same
 210: note) placed their addr, stopped, chkstop and srr0 rows and `T ra me`'s addr and stopped, repair 8's (the same note) the eight
 211: unimpl rows, repair 9's `T blr o1` and `T blr o2`, repair 10's `T blr m1`, `T blr m2` and `T blr m3`, and repair 11's partners `T
 212: rp` .. `T rp o3m`; the other shapes are disclosed below.
 213:   discloses, not claimed: arm (a)'s guard and its exit are claimed only at read-ahead depth 1, the only depth measured -- a
 214: weakening of the guard, or a substitution of its exit (arm (b)'s refresh-and-return in place of the bare return), that differs
 215: from the fix only at a deeper read-ahead is green on every row and is not claimed, and neither is arm (a) on a read-ahead fetch
 216: whose own translation raises an exception (an ISI or 603 IMISS from memory_rw during read-ahead): read-ahead stays inside the page
 217: the dispatch lookup has just translated, so no session produces it (this clause named deeper read-ahead only:
 218: LATE_REPLICATIONS_20261105.md row 35); MSR is rowed on every -T session (from
 219: repair 7: before it `T ra odd` had no msr row and this clause was false -- codex pass 6, R1), and a write to a CPU field this block
 220: neither reads nor writes -- one that changes none of pc, SRR0, MSR or the reports -- is not claimed, nor is a write to SRR1 (only
 221: arm (d)'s machine check writes it here, unreached on pmppc, and no session rows it), and neither is a write to running in arm (a)
 222: (R5_arun, MEASURED green in tables 5, 6 and 7; the repair-pass-4 review): the real fetch's second halt masks it on every read-ahead
 223: session, a window whose last word branches away would see it, and none is measured on pmppc; a mask on the aligned compare that
 224: also clears bits above bit 3 is caught where a cleared bit is one the rowed failing fetch addresses carry -- 0x02040000 bits 18 and
 225: 25, 0x02040004 bits 2, 18 and 25, 0xfec00008 bits 3, 22-23 and 25-31 -- because arm (b) then takes that fetch (MEASURED for bits 2
 226: and 3, R6_mask7 and R6_mask15; DERIVED, not measured, for the others: `~0x40003` against `T blr`, codex pass 6); one whose extra
 227: cleared bits are all absent from those addresses -- bits 4-17, 19-21, 24 or above 31 (`~0x13`, for example) -- changes no rowed
 228: fetch's arm (b) test and is not claimed (this clause said "no rowed failing fetch carries such a bit" of every bit above bit 3,
 229: which those addresses refute: codex pass 6, R2); the read's failure test disjoined with `translation_readahead` (glm, pass 5) is
 230: not claimed: a successful read-ahead fetch then returns through arm (a) untranslated, which costs translation throughput and
 231: changes no guest-visible state; arm (b)'s refresh (D11, V2): repair 5 compares pc with its low two bits cleared, because an
 232: unaligned pc keeps them through the translator's prologue (cpu->pc is assigned before addr is aligned) -- from the debugger, and
 233: from guest code, since this fork's mtlr and its unconditional blr (X(bclr_20)) copy LR without masking them (architecturally a
 234: branch ignores them: filed separately) -- and the bare compare sent such a pc into arm (b), which re-ran the slot (`T blr` rows it
 235: now); arm (b) itself is reached only when the translation moved pc to an exception vector, on no measured session -- so its compare
 236: made `cpu->pc < addr` (R7_G1_b_lt, the Gemini seat's pass 6; MEASURED green, r7_20261105/B123_NOTE.md) is not claimed: wherever the
 237: fix skips arm (b) the aligned pc equals addr and pc is not below it, and the taken side has no producer, because cpu_dyntrans.c's
 238: lookup re-translates every page without host memory and delivers the exception itself before the translator runs -- also when
 239: MSR[IP] puts the vector above the fetch (r7_20261105/g12_table/explore); WITHOUT -T the guest-made unaligned fetch reads zeros and
 240: stops on the zero word, so no arm of the block runs (MEASURED, p4_20261105/AC_NOTE.md) and no no-T `blr` session is rowed; arm (d)
 241: and the checkstop fallback (D6, D9, D10, and R7_G2_d_msr -- arm (d)'s test made `if (cpu->cd.ppc.msr)`, the Gemini seat's pass 6,
 242: MEASURED green; with V4 and V5 green no predicate in that position is observable): no fetch on pmppc reaches them -- MEASURED by a
 243: fetch at every 4-byte offset of every window `device list` names, MSR 0 and MSR[ME], each offset with evidence the word was fetched
 244: (det_20261104/window_sweep.out), and in the slack above RAM (slack_sweep.out); their producer is a device declining an instruction
 245: fetch while running, which needs another machine (the reconciliation's ROW 5, FILED pending X11), and it is the only producer of a
 246: read-ahead fetch that fails with running still 1 -- every rowed read-ahead failure is a -T halt, which clears running before the
 247: read returns -- so arm (a)'s guard conjoined with `!cpu->running` (the Gemini seat's pass-6 replication, G3; not built) is
 248: equivalent on pmppc and not claimed; 64-bit CPUs; PPC603-class CPUs (their miss vector is 0x10); IR-on fetches whose translation
 249: succeeds onto non-existent memory; a successful slow-path fetch with running already 0 (glm's `|| !running` widening of the failure
 250: test) -- no measured single-CPU shape produces one: a -T data halt ends the run at the faulting load or store
 251: (p3_20261105/DHALT_NOTE.md), and the one producer that measurement cannot see is another CPU mid-batch after memory.c's -T halt
 252: cleared every CPU's running (#PPP).  THE READ-AHEAD CELLS are measured on cpc700_pci (the eight sessions `T ra`, `T ra me`, `T ra
 253: odd`, `T ra o1m`, `T ra o2`, `T ra o2m`, `T ra o3`, `T ra o3m`: pc's low two bits x MSR[ME]); at the other seven windows' last
 254: words the word a guest load records before the continue is 0x00000000, which decodes as unimplemented, so no read-ahead past the
 255: window is issued (part 2: no halt report) -- MEASURED at that word, DERIVED for other values of those registers: a window end
 256: inside a page puts the failing word in reach of read-ahead, and whether read-ahead happens depends on the decoded word (cpc700_pci
 257: shows a valid non-branch word reaches it).  Read-ahead runs only on a free-running continue: single-step disables it (measured,
 258: artifacts/qhslowifetch/p2r_20261105/extra_sessions.out), and so do instruction trace and any set breakpoint (cpu_dyntrans.c's
 259: read-ahead condition, by code reading).  The RTC window ran twice and read 0 at +0xfc both times.
 260:   RE-ENTRY -- every exit returns before the slot's function pointer is replaced, so the slot stays untranslated.  Re-entry after
 261: arm (a)'s exit is measured by `T ra`: the slot stays untranslated and the real fetch re-enters the arm in the same batch (the
 262: second report).  Re-entry after arm (c)'s exit is untestable here: the park ends the batch and running is clear, so nothing
 263: fetches the slot again; the `again` session therefore measures nothing about re-entry after a park and stands as the control
 264: that the debugger survives step and continue on a halted CPU, its halt-count row the control that a -T halt is terminal for the
 265: session.  W5's catch rides on the uninitialised instruction word: which rows red under W5 depends on the garbage decoded, though
 266: some row must (a decoded word moves pc, traps or prints UNIMPLEMENTED; one that branches back to its own slot changes nothing on
 267: that session -- `T blr` stays green under R7b_f_me and R7b_f_ra -- so the claim rests on the other sessions).  -T imprecision: a -T
 268: data halt earlier in the same batch followed by a declined fetch takes arm (c), with no machine check (cosmetic; the debugger is
 269: entered either way). The reconciliation's W7 (the read-ahead guard missing) is rowed by `T ra`; its W8 (the running-1 arm missing)
 270: and W9 (a wrong machine check) have no row on pmppc: they need its ROW 5 (FILED pending X11).  On this 249-row probe the pre-fix
 271: build scores 108/249 (141 rows red) with PPC_IFETCH_SYMPTOM=PRESENT, and the three null media -- /bin/true 94/249, an absent binary
 272: 64/249, /bin/false 65/249 -- each CONTROL=FAIL (r7_20261105/table12/SCORES.txt).
 273: 
 274: Sentinel: PPC_IFETCH_PROBE_DONE (plus PPC_IFETCH_RESULT=n/N, PPC_IFETCH_CONTROL=OK|FAIL, PPC_IFETCH_SYMPTOM=PRESENT|ABSENT,
 275: PPC_IFETCH_RED=none|<names>).  Session transcripts go to the optional [workdir].
 276: """
 277: 
 278: import os
 279: import re
 280: import subprocess
 281: import sys
 282: import tempfile
 283: import time
 284: 
 285: if len(sys.argv) < 2:
 286:     sys.stderr.write("usage: ppc_ifetch_probe.py <gxemul> [label] [workdir]\n")
 287:     sys.exit(2)
 288: 
 289: BIN = sys.argv[1]
 535:     regs, T, how = session(nm, ["srr0=0x%x" % SENT] + (["msr=0x%x" % msr] if msr else []) + ["pc=0x%x" % (RA_LAST | low), "continue"],
 536:                            flags=["-T"])
 537:     row(nm + " session", how, "exit0", "-T read-ahead, pc&3 = %d, ME %s: survives" % (low, "set" if msr else "clear"))
 538:     row(nm + " pc", hexr(regs, "pc"), hex(RA_NEXT | low), "parked past the window, low bits kept (R7_fail_unal)")
 539:     row(nm + " nonex", nonex(T), "2", "arm (a) returns at this cell (%s)" % kills)
 540:     row(nm + " addr", halts(T), hex(RA_NEXT), "every halt names the word past the window (W2, D3)")
 541:     row(nm + " stopped", stopped(T), "yes", "the -T halt stopped the machine (B1)")
 542:     row(nm + " msr", hexr(regs, "msr"), hex(msr), "MSR as entered (%s)" % ("R7_a_msrclr" if msr else "R7_a_msrset"))
 543:     row(nm + " chkstop", chk(T), "absent", "no checkstop line on this route (R7b_a_chkun)")
 544:     row(nm + " srr0", hexr(regs, "srr0"), hex(SENT), "no exception invented on this route (R7b_a_srr0un)")
 545:     row(nm + " unimpl", unimpl(T), "absent",
 546:         "the real fetch is not sent to bad: (%s)" % ("W3, V10, R8_c_meun_bad" if msr else "W3, R8_c_clun_bad"))
 547: # THE ONE-ENTRY PARTNERS (repair 11; codex pass 10, B1; r7_20261105/B123_NOTE.md).  Each read-ahead session enters the failure block
 548: # TWICE at one full pc -- the read-ahead visit, then the real fetch; its partner enters it ONCE at the SAME full pc and MSR: pc set to
 549: # 0xfec00008 | low bits directly and continued under -T, so the first fetch fails (a failed fetch is never translated, so no
 550: # read-ahead follows) and arm (c) parks it.  The pair then presents the block with the same pc, addr, MSR, running (0) and slot; only
 551: # translation_readahead differs, nonzero on the two-entry session's first visit.  So a toggle conditioned on any of those that the
 552: # toggle itself leaves unchanged fires on both visits exactly when it fires on the partner's one -- it cancels on the pair's two-entry
 553: # side and shows on the partner -- and a condition on translation_readahead fires on one visit only and shows on the two-entry side.
 554: # A self-referential toggle is outside this: the docstring's SCOPE (codex pass 11, R1).
 555: for tag, low, msr in (("", 0, 0), ("me", 0, MSR_ME), ("odd", 1, 0), ("o1m", 1, MSR_ME), ("o2", 2, 0), ("o2m", 2, MSR_ME),
 556:                       ("o3", 3, 0), ("o3m", 3, MSR_ME)):
 557:     nm, pair = ("T rp " + tag).rstrip(), ("T ra " + tag).rstrip()
 558:     regs, T, how = session(nm, ["srr0=0x%x" % SENT] + (["msr=0x%x" % msr] if msr else []) + ["pc=0x%x" % (RA_NEXT | low), "continue"],
 559:                            flags=["-T"])
 560:     row(nm + " session", how, "exit0", "-T fetch at %s's full pc, one entry: survives" % pair)
 561:     row(nm + " pc", hexr(regs, "pc"), hex(RA_NEXT | low), "parked at the same full pc as %s's real fetch" % pair)
 562:     row(nm + " nonex", nonex(T), "1", "ONE halt report: one entry, where %s has two (R6_mask15)" % pair)
 563:     row(nm + " addr", halts(T), hex(RA_NEXT), "the halt names the same word as %s's (W2, D3)" % pair)
 564:     row(nm + " stopped", stopped(T), "yes", "the -T halt stopped the machine (B1)")
 565:     row(nm + " msr", hexr(regs, "msr"), hex(msr), "MSR as entered: one entry, no toggle cancels (R9_tog_me%d)" % low)
 566:     row(nm + " chkstop", chk(T), "absent", "arm (c) parked it; no checkstop (%s)" % ("V11" if msr else "D1, D2"))
 567:     row(nm + " srr0", hexr(regs, "srr0"), hex(SENT),
 568:         "SRR0 as entered: one entry, no toggle cancels (R11_tog_full, R11_tog_full_%d%s)" % (low, "m" if msr else "c"))
 569:     row(nm + " unimpl", unimpl(T), "absent", "the halt is not sent to bad: (W3%s)" % (", V10" if msr else ""))
 570: # Arm (b) with a guest-made UNALIGNED pc (repair pass 4; p4_20261105/BLR_NOTE.md, ADJ_MYTHOS.md): this fork's mtlr and its
 571: # unconditional blr (X(bclr_20)) copy LR unmasked and the translator's prologue aligns addr but not pc, so `mtlr r3; blr` reaches the
 572: # failure block with pc != addr.  Before repair 5 arm (b) took it, refreshed and re-ran the slot: 8278 halt reports under -T.  With
 573: # the aligned compare the fetch parks in arm (c).  r3 = 0x02040007 has bits 0-2 set (repair 6; p5_20261105/MASK7_NOTE.md): the
 574: # prologue gives addr 0x02040004, so a mask narrowed to either low bit (`& ~1`, `& ~2`) or widened to bit 2 (`& ~7`) still floods.
 575: # The program is written with `put b` (byte stores do not warm translations); a far breakpoint disables read-ahead.
 576: BLR_PC = 0x02040007
 577: cmds = ["srr0=0x%x" % SENT, "r3=0x%x" % BLR_PC]
 578: for i, w in enumerate((0x7C6803A6, 0x4E800020)):          # mtlr r3 ; blr
 579:     for j in range(4):
 580:         cmds.append("put b 0x%x,0x%02x" % (ENTRY + 4 * i + j, (w >> (24 - 8 * j)) & 0xff))
 581: regs, T, how = session("T blr", cmds + ["breakpoint add 0x3000", "continue"], flags=["-T"])
 582: row("T blr session", how, "exit0", "-T fetch at a guest-made unaligned pc: survives")
 583: row("T blr pc", hexr(regs, "pc"), hex(BLR_PC), "parked at the unaligned pc (arm (c))")
 584: row("T blr nonex", nonex(T), "1", "one halt report: the slot is not re-run (repair 5)")
 585: row("T blr srr0", hexr(regs, "srr0"), hex(SENT), "no exception invented")
 275:     check "ppc_llsc SYMPTOM=ABSENT"  "$(grep -cx 'PPC_LLSC_SYMPTOM=ABSENT' "$LLSCLOG")" "1"
