 287: # ---- qhslowifetch (#NNN): a failed slow-path instruction fetch no longer ends the emulator process -- its 249-row detector ------
 288: # X(to_be_translated) read the word with memory_rw and, on failure, printed `read failed: TODO' and called exit(1).  The arm now
 289: # returns on read-ahead, refreshes next_ic when the translation already delivered an exception, PARKS the CPU on a -T halt, and
 290: # delivers a machine check (MSR[ME] set) or a checkstop (clear) when a device declines the fetch while running.  `-E pmppc' with a
 291: # raw four-byte word needs no image, so this block runs BEFORE the NetBSD prerequisite, like the #579 block above.  Thirty-one cold
 292: # sessions: controls (a live word, a bogus machine, the ISI route by continue and by step, the no -T route), four -T sessions at
 293: # 0x02040000 -- step, continue, step-step-continue-continue, and a step with MSR[ME] set -- each pinning the park (pc, SRR0), the
 294: # exact halt-report count, the final MSR and the absence of the fatal, UNIMPLEMENTED, exception and checkstop text (the ME-set
 295: # step pins the same), eight -T continues from cpc700_pci's last word whose read-ahead reaches arm (a) -- pc's low two bits {00,
 296: # 01, 10, 11} x MSR[ME] {clear, set}, entered at 0xfec00004 | low bits, each pinning the same nine channels: survival, the park pc,
 297: # the two halt reports, the halted address, the stop, the final MSR, no checkstop line, SRR0 untouched and no UNIMPLEMENTED text
 298: # (repair 7 completed the grid, repairs 7b and 8 the channels; repair 6 added the first unaligned cell), eight one-entry PARTNERS
 299: # at the same full pc and MSR as those eight (pc set to 0xfec00008 | low bits directly, so the first fetch fails once; repair 11):
 300: # each pair presents the failure block with the same pc, addr, MSR, running and slot and differs only in translation_readahead, so a
 301: # toggle that cancels over the two-entry session's two visits, under a condition on state the block reads that the toggle itself
 302: # leaves unchanged, shows once on its partner (scope: the probe's docstring; codex pass 11, R1) -- and six -T continues
 303: # into a guest-made unaligned pc (mtlr; blr), low bits 11, 01 and 10 with MSR[ME] clear and set, that arm (c) must park: one-entry
 304: # failures, which see a change the block makes under pc's low bits and ME that the two-entry read-ahead sessions undo (repairs 5,
 305: # 6, 9 and 10; with `T cont`, `T step`, `again` and `T me` they give every (low bits, ME) cell a one-entry session).
 306: # The rung-3 witness is the 17-row probe frozen at regress/artifacts/qhslowifetch/witness_20261104/; the detector scores 108/249 (141
 307: # rows red) on the pre-fix build and 249/249 on the fix (regress/artifacts/qhslowifetch/r7_20261105/table12/SCORES.txt).  Scored in the
 308: # #579 shape: the completion sentinel once and last; each protocol key once in any form and once accepted; every row by name; the
 309: # emitted, green and red row counts pinned to literals.  Names are at most 16 characters in an 18-wide column.  Test-variant tables:
 310: # regress/artifacts/qhslowifetch/det_20261104/table1/ (the 50-row probe), table2/ (the 56-row probe), r3_20261105/table3/
 311: # (the 62-row probe), r4_20261105/table4/ (the 69-row probe), r5_20261105/table5/ (the 79-row probe), r6_20261105/table6/ (the
 312: # 82-row probe), r7_20261105/table7/ (the 103-row probe), r7_20261105/table8/ (the 129-row probe), r7_20261105/table9/ (the 137-row
 313: # probe), r7_20261105/table10/ (the 153-row probe), r7_20261105/table11/ (the 177-row probe) and r7_20261105/table12/ (this probe,
 314: # the record; its pairing check, table12/PAIRS_base.out).
 315: IFLOG=$LOGDIR/ppc_ifetch.log
 316: python3 -u ppc_ifetch_probe.py "$PMAX" gate "$LOGDIR/ppc_ifetch" > "$IFLOG" 2>&1 || true
 317: if [ "$(grep -cx 'PPC_IFETCH_PROBE_DONE' "$IFLOG")" != 1 ]; then
