2682: > over a live total escape.** The breach that pass 3 found was not in that pass's two hunks --
2683: > the hunks were fine. It lived in the SHIPPED COMPOSITE detector's coverage of the ORIGINAL
2684: > fix's mutant space.
2685: >
2686: > > **Review EFFORT is scoped to the repair diff, so settled design is not re-litigated. The
2687: > > FLOOR QUESTION -- does a clean-sweep mutant exist in the (d) enumeration -- is asked of the
2688: > > SHIPPED COMPOSITE on every pass.**
2689: >
2690: > #### THE BOUND IS IMPORTED, NOT INTRINSIC -- state the dependency or the rule overclaims
2691: >
2692: > The stop condition does not bound the chain and must not pretend to. The bound comes from
2693: > **the (d) DEPENDS-ON enumeration being diff-closed and finite**, and from *zero breaches*
2694: > meaning **zero SURVIVING ADJUDICATION** rather than zero raised -- otherwise one stubborn
2695: > seat blocks closure forever, against the count-arguments-not-seats rule. With those imports
2696: > the chain is infinite only if every repair is defective, in which case every pass is buying a
2697: > real defect off the ship.
2698: >
2699: > #### *** THE AMENDMENT THAT ACTUALLY ENDS CHAINS, and it is the part worth carrying. ***
2700: >
2701: > `#499`'s three breaches were **THE SAME CLASS THREE TIMES** -- a cell of one state space left
2702: > empty, repaired at exactly the address the mutant had used, leaving the symmetric cell open
2703: > for the next pass. Pass 1 found *width* unpinned; pass 2 found *component*; pass 3 found
2704: > *direction* AND *position*. **Pass-per-instance converges LINEARLY IN CELLS**, and 28 -> 34
2705: > -> 36 rows bought one cell each.
2706: >
2707: > > **WHEN TWO CONSECUTIVE PASSES FIND BREACHES OF ONE CLASS, THE NEXT REPAIR OWES THE CLASS
2708: > > CLOSURE: enumerate the full space from the function's own inputs, close every cell in ONE
2709: > > diff, and write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not.
2710: > > The closing pass then VERIFIES THE ENUMERATION rather than hunting cells.**
2711: >
2712: > That is the reading-seat-buys-the-class lesson wearing the repair hat. It also converts a
2713: > future escape from *"another breach"* into *"outside the contract, as stated"* -- which is
2714: > exactly what clause (e) is for, and which a cell-by-cell chain can never reach.
