 522: # unrowed, so the read-ahead route is crossed over pc's low two bits {00, 01, 10, 11} x MSR[ME] {clear, set}: `T ra`, `T ra me` and
 523: # `T ra odd` hold three cells and these five sessions the rest -- `T ra` entered at 0xfec00004 | low bits, MSR written only when ME
 524: # is set (`m`).  The prologue keeps pc's low bits, so the read-ahead fetch reaches the failure block at pc 0xfec00008 | low bits; arm
 525: # (a) returns, the subfic runs, the real fetch halts again and arm (c) parks at that pc: exit 0, that pc, two reports naming
 526: # 0xfec00008, the stop, MSR as entered, no checkstop line, SRR0 untouched and no UNIMPLEMENTED text -- `T ra`'s nine channels
 527: # (repair 7b; `unimpl`, repair 8).  A guard that refuses a cell parks it at read-ahead time instead (one report); an MSR or SRR0
 528: # write, a checkstop print, or a transfer to bad: from the real fetch (where bad: prints UNIMPLEMENTED and changes nothing else; a
