The low-bit catch is supported by the rows: a marker-set entry clears the bit once, and the exact final-PC check detects it. The next_ic correction also matches the code. I’m checking one remaining edge in R1: whether an unchanged condition is enough to guarantee both visits if the toggle changes the pc’s page.
